#
# Component:       repo
# Module:          scripts/lib/doc-definitions.psv
# Owning Team:     Platform Enablement Guild (PEG)
# Classification:  INTERNAL
# Purpose:         Top-level definitions that scripts/doc-check.sh requires to
#                  be preceded by a comment (CLAUDE.md 6.5.4, "remaining
#                  languages"), per header type. A row is added together with
#                  the first file of a language that has no native coverage
#                  tool.
# Related Docs:    scripts/doc-check.sh, ADR-0009
#
# Columns: type|definition|comment|skip|inline
#   type        Header type from templates/headers/styles.psv.
#   definition  POSIX ERE matching a line that starts a top-level definition.
#   comment     ERE matching a comment line; the nearest preceding line that
#               is not matched by `skip` must match it.
#   skip        ERE of lines allowed between the comment and the definition
#               (attributes, decorators, .PHONY); empty when none.
#   inline      ERE that documents the definition on its own line (for
#               example `## help` after a make target); empty when none.
# Patterns may not contain `|`; use bracket expressions instead.
shell|^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*[(][)][[:space:]]*[{]|^[[:space:]]*#||
make|^[A-Za-z0-9_%][A-Za-z0-9_%./-]*:([^=].*)?$|^#|^[.]PHONY:|##[[:space:]]
sql|^DEFINE [A-Z]+ |^--||COMMENT "
